{"title":"1980 USAMO Problems/Problem 4","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1980_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The insphere of a tetrahedron touches each face at its centroid. Show that the tetrahedron is regular.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1980_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> be the tetrahedron, and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/9866e3a998d628ba0941eb4fea0666ac391d149a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" /> be the points at which the insphere touches faces <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/a/a6adfd3ad27a2dddeb0af7131d73c33c86991e93.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" /> respectively (and therefore the centroids of those faces). Looking at the plane containing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/9866e3a998d628ba0941eb4fea0666ac391d149a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" />, we see that the intersection of the sphere and the plane is a circle, and that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/b/e3bb4eeb347e74e025fd175c22f1f7275af0555e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AP$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/6/7563031eab26ad18658cf2f6a8e4948861bb9013.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AQ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> are both tangent to said circle. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/2/f6235de9bde9e47652ee5f3cfbad1a2666873220.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[AP]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"36\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/b/90b276b00258efc6015a7c62e6f8c1edad3cd77d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[AQ]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"36\" height=\"18\" /> are tangents to the circle from the same point and thus have the same length. The same goes for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/a/cda0272ae887e314ff58215fbf55333fa558fefd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[BP]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/9/88983a4a2386c3da803defe0794cc5c72fe5748b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[BQ]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" />. Thus, triangles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/b/a7b510ddc7cf8a87b5cc0dd15adf8480cd2e6945.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABP$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/9/569d168dce2c902daf7fc9a6b79a275caef81a0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABQ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"42\" height=\"16\" /> are congruent, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/b/7db6330df5c0091df22528473740c9e7c4d731a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathbf{\\angle PAB = \\angle QAB}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"141\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>Let the intersection of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/b/e3bb4eeb347e74e025fd175c22f1f7275af0555e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AP$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" />, and let the intersection of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/6/7563031eab26ad18658cf2f6a8e4948861bb9013.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AQ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/f/89fff82bb65d0215e49c8c91cb7c553da52205e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/3/e73bc78b745edf7fe1e55dbfc3d914190faf5015.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AM$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"35\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/a/9aafc7e3cc1eafce5e16d3a45250eeda7b1a6526.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AN$\" width=\"30\" height=\"13\" /> are medians of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/a/a6adfd3ad27a2dddeb0af7131d73c33c86991e93.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" />, and thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/1/4e1d26919fe3b4cf3e25905158af12065255e70e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|AM| = \\frac{3}{2}|AP| = \\frac{3}{2}|AQ| = |AN|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"260\" height=\"38\" />. We already know from the previous congruence that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/d/bad0947da4d39d6b94f60e590d9f359e6906deed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{MAB} = \\angle{PAB} = \\angle{QAB} = \\angle{NAB}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"304\" height=\"18\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/0/2e0642ba0f9c6c6e9422d7c68a48a7e0129c10d0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|AB|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"36\" height=\"18\" /> is equal to itself. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/4/2a40fcf0618c04c1e439daacc736708fdfb94d1b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MAB$\" width=\"47\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/9/a593eb7e988de7384d8591912db0935fbe09f464.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$NAB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"47\" height=\"14\" /> are also congruent to each other. Finally, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/2/c52cffa58d71ea5b58ac3fee6afe538c06369e77.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|BC| = 2|BM| = 2|BN| = |BD|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"258\" height=\"20\" /> (Because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> are midpoints of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/f/89fff82bb65d0215e49c8c91cb7c553da52205e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> respectively), and from the congruence of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/4/2a40fcf0618c04c1e439daacc736708fdfb94d1b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MAB$\" width=\"47\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/9/a593eb7e988de7384d8591912db0935fbe09f464.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$NAB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"47\" height=\"14\" /> we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/d/f7d24a7af4d6f27a19178103ac0eea166329da91.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{CBA} = \\angle{MBA} = \\angle{NBA} = \\angle{DBA}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"305\" height=\"14\" />, and again <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/0/2e0642ba0f9c6c6e9422d7c68a48a7e0129c10d0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|AB|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"36\" height=\"18\" /> is equal to itself. Thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/a/a6adfd3ad27a2dddeb0af7131d73c33c86991e93.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" /> are congruent, thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/b/92bd53905a57e6fe5dbeb4b08989c9c2c97fe9b0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathbf{|AC| = |AD|}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"108\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/0/820183d6857a655a30f49a927245f44a00181e3d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathbf{|BC| = |BD|}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"107\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>By applying the same logic to faces <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/a/d7ada763e99852a6e44a15d46cce3c3709a944d5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/e/6ce2cd123db24a7b8373999aea7a98927e3b3c81.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ACD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" /> we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/5/7d5838b6408905b250ca5b924a73d57c2dec82e9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|AC| = |BC|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"103\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/a/3ba4e20bcc77ed42d74b99c44e330368a3f339cf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|AD| = |BD|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"106\" height=\"20\" />. Finally, applying the same logic to faces <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/3/21361fc8f29984fa3e95bfc0e578efdbce08c736.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ACB$\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/e/6ce2cd123db24a7b8373999aea7a98927e3b3c81.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ACD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" /> we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/3/143ef8413eef4ec3149c343fe38992c6c26e215a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|AB| = |AD|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"104\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/b/59b9305c45ec1efcc510010ce7a00847f3e50fe6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|CB| = |CD|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"105\" height=\"20\" />. Putting all these equalities together, we get that all edges of the tetrahedron are equal, and thus the tetrahedron is regular. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/b/3bbb9e25e5be095e317771a9c5d00877ee9c8012.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\blacksquare$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1980_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:40%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1980_USAMO\" title=\"1980 USAMO\">1980 USAMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1980_USAMO_Problems\" title=\"1980 USAMO Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=27&amp;year=1980\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1980_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1980 USAMO Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1980_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1980 USAMO Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1980_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1980 USAMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1980_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1980 USAMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1980_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1980 USAMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1980_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1980 USAMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=USAMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"USAMO Problems and Solutions\"> All USAMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017173418\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.035 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.058 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 312/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1267/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 44/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 9493/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   12.725      1 -total\n 54.83%    6.977      1 Template:USAMO_box\n 42.77%    5.442      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:11415:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017173418 and revision id 191126. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}